const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"工作论文考察外部董事是否会在预期公司表现不佳或出现负面披露时辞职。 阅读时应把它理解为受样本、时点和制度限定的问题，而不是可以脱离条件的结论。",en:"The working paper examines whether outside directors have incentives to resign when they anticipate poor firm performance or adverse disclosure. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.3386/w15917",label:{zh:"National Bureau of Economic Research Working Paper 15917 (2010) · 来源说明",en:"National Bureau of Economic Research Working Paper 15917 (2010) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"它研究意外董事离任，并比较受影响公司之后的股价、经营、重述和诉讼相关结果。 比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系共同构成研究合同；改变其中一项，可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It studies surprise director departures and compares affected firms' subsequent stock, operating, restatement, and litigation-related outcomes described in the paper's abstract. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.3386/w15917",label:{zh:"National Bureau of Economic Research Working Paper 15917 (2010) · 来源说明",en:"National Bureau of Economic Research Working Paper 15917 (2010) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"忠实延伸需要带日期的董事会成员和离任分类、公司身份、价格与经营指标、重述及诉讼记录和原文事件定义。 字段定义、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原研究分别记录，不能仅因变量同名或使用最新修订值就视为可比。",en:"A faithful extension needs dated board membership and departure classifications, firm identifiers, price and operating measures, restatement and lawsuit records, and the paper's event definitions. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.3386/w15917",label:{zh:"National Bureau of Economic Research Working Paper 15917 (2010) · 来源说明",en:"National Bureau of Economic Research Working Paper 15917 (2010) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"来源报告意外离任后的相关性；一次离任本身不是不当行为、预知信息或公司治理结论的证据。 它只支持来源所描述的经验或理论关系，不能把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The source reports associations after surprise departures; a departure is not by itself evidence of misconduct, foreknowledge, or a firm-specific governance verdict. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not turn association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.3386/w15917",label:{zh:"National Bureau of Economic Research Working Paper 15917 (2010) · 来源说明",en:"National Bureau of Economic Research Working Paper 15917 (2010) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"区分预期和意外离任；保留公告与生效日期；核对董事身份和角色；在观察结果前预先定义所有窗口。 开展后续分析前，应将这些选择写入版本化研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Separate anticipated from surprise exits; preserve announcement versus effective dates; verify director identity and board role; define all outcome windows before inspecting results. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.3386/w15917",label:{zh:"National Bureau of Economic Research Working Paper 15917 (2010) · 来源说明",en:"National Bureau of Economic Research Working Paper 15917 (2010) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 National Bureau of Economic Research Working Paper 15917 (2010)。历史样本和事件分类不支持对任何董事或公司作出当前法律、合规或投资结论。 如需数值结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites National Bureau of Economic Research Working Paper 15917 (2010). The paper's historical sample and event classification do not support a current legal, compliance, or investment conclusion about any director or company. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.3386/w15917",label:{zh:"National Bureau of Economic Research Working Paper 15917 (2010) · 来源说明",en:"National Bureau of Economic Research Working Paper 15917 (2010) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“The Dark Side of Outside Directors: Do They Quit When They Are Most Needed?”公开说明的研究对象与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。历史样本和事件分类不支持对任何董事或公司作出当前法律、合规或投资结论。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “The Dark Side of Outside Directors: Do They Quit When They Are Most Needed?”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
